senses.gloss:
श्व॑भ्र m. n. fissure of the earth, pit, hole;
 m. hell, a
man's name.

2 श्व॑स् adv. to-morrow, next day;
 श्वः श्वस् from day to day,
daily.

श्व॑स्तन a. of to-morrow;
 n. & f. ई the tomorrow or
next day.

स्व॑ (poss. refl.) one's own (often ˚—). m. n. one's self (in
the obl. cases also used as a pronoun, cf. आत्मन्);
 m. & f. आ a
kinsman or relation, a man or woman of one's own caste;
 n. property,
wealth, riches.

स्वान्त m. one's own end or death, kingdom or country;
 n.
the heart (as the dominion of the self).

श्वास m. hissing, snorting;
 breath, esp. breathing in;
aspiration (g.);
 sighing, sigh.

स्वक (poss. refl.) = prec.;
 m. relative, friend;
 n. wealth,
property.

स्वकीय (poss. refl.) one's own;
 m. pl. relatives or
friends.

स्वगत a. relating or belonging to one's self;
 n. adv.
apart, aside.

स्वागत a. welcome (also lit. well come i.e. well
acquired);
 n. welcome, salutation, ˚ती कृ make into a welcome.

स्वगा॑ (indecl.) a sacrificial formula;
 w. कृ utter this
exclamation.

स्वच्छ a. very clear, transparent, bright, pure;
 abstr.
˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

1 स्वतन्त्र n. self-dependence, i.e. independence,
freedom;
 also ˚ता f.

स्वद् स्व॑दति स्व॑द˚ते (स्वादते), pp. स्वात्त॑
(q.v.) A. sweeten, make savoury or agreeable;
 A. (P.) be sweet or
savoury, please;
 relish, taste, eat, enjoy;
 delight in (loc.). C.
स्वदयति make savoury, season, cook;
 make soft i.e. calm, propitiate;
स्वादयति relish, taste, eat. — आ & समा (स्वादयति) relish, eat,
enjoy.

2 स्वधा॑ f. sweet drink, esp. a libation to the Manes;
 the
exclamation Svadhā (used on presenting or instead of this libation).

स्व॑पस् a. working or worked well, skilful or skilfully
made;
 m. artist.

स्व॑प्न्य n. vision of a dream;
 स्वप्न्य॑या adv. in
dreaming.

स्वभाव m. birth-place;
 (one's own) inherent disposition
or nature;
 ˚—, abl., & instr. by nature, naturally, spontaneously.

स्वभू a. self-existing;
 m. Brahman;
 f. one's own country
or home.

स्वयंकृत॑ a. self-made;
 done by or for one's self;
made one's own, adopted.

स्वयं॑कृत a. self-made;
 done by or for one's self;
made one's own, adopted.

2 स्वयंग्राह a. taking freely or violently;
 ˚— & n.
adv. voluntarily, spontaneously.

स्वायत्त a. subject to one's self, standing under one's
own control;
 abstr. ˚त्व n.

स्वय॑म् (indecl.) self (applied to the gramm. or log.
subject);
 often ˚— self-, spontaneously, voluntarily, naturally.

स्वयंप्रकाशमान a. self-luminous;
 abstr.
˚त्व n.

स्व॑युक्ति f. one's own team;
 one's own arrangement or
disposition, instr. & ˚तस्† naturally, of course.

स्वरसंयोग m. = स्वरयोग;
 also song or playing
on the lute.*

स्वरित a. sounded, accented, having the Sv. accent;
 m. n.
the Svarita accent;
 abstr. ˚त्व n.

स्वरूप n. (one's own) form or shape, true nature, p.
स्वरूप˚वन्त् & स्वरू˚पिन्;
 (±शब्द˚ or शब्दस्य) the word in its
peculiar form, the word itself (g.);
 ˚— & ˚तस् by nature, of one's
self, really.

स्वर्जि॑त् a. conquering light or heaven;
 m. a kind of
sacrifice.

2 स्वार्थ a. relating to one's own person, self-interested,
egoistic;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

स्वर्भानव m. a kind of stone;
 f. ई N. of a
daughter of Svarbhānu.

स्वर्मीळ्ह n. or as adj. w. आजि m. the contest for
light;
 contest, fight i.g.

स्वल्प a. very small or minute, insignificant;
 instr. for a
very short time. Compar. ˚तर & स्वल्पीयंस्.

स्वस्तिक m. a kind of bard (calling hail!);
 N. of a
serpent-demon etc.;
 any lucky or auspicious figure, esp. the figure of a
cross, a dish of a cert. form, the crossing of the arms;
 a building
shaped like a cross (also n.).

स्वस्तिकार m. bard, herald (cf. prec.);
 the exclamation
स्वस्ति.

स्वस्तिवाच्य a. to be called upon to pronounce a
benediction;
 n. = स्वस्तिवाचन.

स्वस्त्य॑यन n. good progress, success, welfare,
blessing, benediction;
 a. (f. ई) producing happiness.

स्वस्थ a. being in one's natural condition, healthy,
well, comfortable;
 abstr. ˚ता f.

स्वहित a. good for or kind to one's self;
 n. one's own
welfare.

स्वाच्छन्द्य n. independence, liberty;
 instr.
willingly, of one's own accord.

स्वातन्त्र्य n. self-dependence, free will;
 instr.
spontaneously, freely.

स्वा॑दन a. making savoury, sweetening, seasoning;
 n.
tasting, relishing.

स्वादु॑ f. ˚द्वी॑ tasting good, savoury, sweet, sweeter than
(abl.);
 n. = seq.

स्वाधीन a. self-dependent, free;
 under one's own
control, subject to one's own will. Abstr. ˚ता f.
